@startuml audit-transport
' Revision 2026-10-12: R-OPERATOR separates signing authority from the analyzer launch account.
title Audit transport - CLI secret input accepted first; backend/cache contracts proposed; current null backend is static-only
actor "Human audit caller / publisher" as O
participant "Curator CLI / manager\naudit caller UID; policy/process/decision owner" as M
participant "Opened private token handle\npublisher-owned file; transient, non-inheritable" as F
participant "Shared agents-management launch layer\nnative argv/settings owner" as L
participant "Selected analyzer child\nmanager-launched identity; direct-child policy" as A
database "Manager-owned private state\nfrozen snapshot, bounded workdir/output\nverdict cache and registry trust/high-water" as S
participant "Registry HTTP service\nsigned record publication owner" as R

note right of O
  R-OPERATOR: swarma-operator never hosts an analyzer/harness session.
  Operator signing authority stays separate from this audit caller/publisher account.
  Operator acts use the phone-signed exact-act main path or password sudo fallback;
  widening authenticates + confirms and refuses agent sessions; narrowing authenticates only.
  Operator reads (status/grants/accounts/bindings) use swarma-observer without confirmation.
  This registry bearer input never becomes an operator device key or broker root.
  [[../CIP-0011-credential-broker-and-agent-users.md#5-curator-broker Operator custody and act rules]]
end note

== Registry publishing secret input; no backend credential propagation ==
O -> M: audit --publish record --registry URL; optional token-file path (never token value)
break legacy --token / -token, repeated file option or wrong-subcommand file input
  M --> O: usage refusal before config/read/launch/network; do not echo raw argv/value
end
alt explicit token file
  M -> F: no-follow, nonblocking open; validate opened type/identity/privacy on same handle
  break link/reparse point, nonregular object, unsafe ACL/privacy or indeterminate read
    M --> O: publication error; no CURATOR_REGISTRY_TOKEN fallback
  end
  F --> M: bounded bytes (65536 raw cap; read at most 65537); remove at most one LF/CRLF
  M -> F: close before publication; handle never inherited by child
else no file option
  M -> M: use CURATOR_REGISTRY_TOKEN; same grammar/cap; no newline removal
end
break missing/empty/oversize/non-ASCII/invalid bearer grammar
  M --> O: source/category only; no contents/headers in diagnostic
end
M -> R: HTTP Bearer publication + signed record; token stays outside argv/config/cache/plans
R --> M: publication result; failure reported, no backend/source fallback

== Audit analysis proposal; independent from publish-token input ==
O -> M: selected audit policy + frozen subject; profile operations strict
M -> S: obtain exact snapshot/current revocation/policy; local static canary before cache authorization
break failed/partial snapshot/cache read, indeterminate identity or static canary failure
  M --> O: block both modes; no absence-triggered fallback / empty success
end
alt null backend
  M --> O: deterministic findings; static-only coverage; no analyzer child
else selected descriptor
  M -> M: validate selected descriptor, executable, bounds and cloud policy
  alt unavailable before canary starts
    M --> O: strict blocks; advisory warns incomplete; no successful backend cache
  else malformed descriptor or unsafe launch plan
    M --> O: error in both modes; no child
  else selected backend admitted
    M -> M: cloud requires allow_cloud and public classification of every contributing identity
    break egress disallowed / redaction incomplete or residual supported secret shape
      M --> O: block both modes; no subject bytes sent, no cloud canary if cloud disabled
    end
    M -> S: inspect eligible successful cache identity; current gates still apply
    alt eligible cache hit
      S --> M: bounded cached findings/coverage and exact adapter/source identity
      M --> O: cached status, not executed in this operation
    else absent or old-version ineligible cache
      M -> L: native audit-purpose plan (Codex/Claude); command kind uses admitted absolute argv
      L --> M: sole native flag/settings construction; unsupported controls refuse
      M -> M: fresh non-nil child env: base/per-kind allowlist; deny *_TOKEN, *_KEY, SSH_AUTH_SOCK, GIT_*
      break required env forbidden / native auth and context suppression unqualified
        M --> O: unsupported; no widening, credential copy or shell fallback
      end
      M -> A: bounded synthetic canary via same runner/adapter/environment, private workdir, stdin
      A --> M: structured canary response
      break started canary timeout/nonzero/malformed or wrong/missing expected findings
        M --> O: block both modes; no extraction/cache pass
      end
      break request exceeds cap after wrapping/redaction
        M --> O: strict blocks; advisory warns incomplete; no extraction/cache pass
      end
      M -> A: whole frozen source as bounded stdin; never checkout execution or source/auth argv
      A --> M: bounded response/stdout (1 MiB), diagnostic stderr (64 KiB), validated identity/findings
      alt timeout/nonzero/malformed/oversize/bad identity
        M -> A: terminate owned tree, drain and reap within deadline
        M --> O: strict blocks; advisory warns incomplete; retain deterministic findings
      else valid bounded findings
        M -> M: manager deterministic verifier decides verifiability; model claim is not authority
        M -> S: bounded atomic cache write unless dry-run
        alt cache persistence fails
          M --> O: valid in-memory result + cache-write diagnostic; no persistence claim
        else cache persisted or dry-run skipped write
          M --> O: decision + backend/adapter/model/cache status + measured coverage; unknown when unmeasured
        end
      end
    end
  end
end
note over M,S
  Canary, egress, revocation and unsafe configuration cannot be waived by pins/fail_on=off.
  Dry-run persists no verdict/pin/response/prompt/auth copy. Git transport has separate auth policy.
  Analyzer saved login is explicitly provisioned; no token passed from registry publication.
  Direct-child environment filtering is not a sandbox or descendant/native-store secrecy claim.
  New backend/cache versions and native qualification unspecified in spec CIP-0005 Open questions.
  [[../CIP-0005-audit-backends-and-cli-secret-transport.md#1-registry-token-sources CIP-0005 token input]]
  [[../CIP-0005-audit-backends-and-cli-secret-transport.md#recommendation CIP-0005 backend/canary/cache]]
  [[../CIP-0005-audit-backends-and-cli-secret-transport.md#6-failure-and-coverage-semantics CIP-0005 refusal semantics]]
end note
@enduml
